Subject: Raw Source Selection for Cantor M2B Platform Preflight Forms

Captured: 2026-07-30
Conversation: cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
Source type: manager-selected dependency-ready slice after completed-work review

Preserve this source separately from canonical and exploded specifications.

The completed no-call Windows ABI probe proves that the exact generated
declarations are available. It does not define a sufficiently strict machine
record for the first target-host platform observation and it does not authorize
calling those declarations.

Select one pure safe-Rust slice before any physical preflight:

- define profile cantor-windows-platform-preflight/0.1;
- admit only the initial target triple x86_64-pc-windows-msvc;
- validate an initial lexical root only in canonical extended-DOS drive form;
- model three closed outcomes:
  1. open_fault, containing the attempted root and nonzero Win32 error;
  2. query_fault, containing the attempted root, one closed failed stage, and
     nonzero Win32 error, with no partial observations;
  3. complete, containing strong root identity, canonical volume-GUID final
     path, complete volume information, remote-protocol information, and one
     disposition;
- reuse StrongFileIdentity and the exact volume-GUID path grammar from the
  proven TopologyReceipt 0.2 vocabulary;
- define query stages for FileIdInfo, final volume-GUID path, volume
  information, and remote-protocol information;
- define complete volume information as volume name, 32-bit
  operating-system-assigned serial, maximum component length, filesystem
  flags, and filesystem name;
- define remote information as structure version, structure size, protocol,
  protocol version tuple, and flags, excluding reserved bytes;
- define dispositions:
  - eligible_local_ntfs only when filesystem name is exactly NTFS and a
    successful remote-protocol observation reports protocol zero;
  - reject_remote_protocol only when the successful remote observation reports
    a nonzero protocol;
  - reject_unsupported_file_system only when remote protocol is zero and the
    filesystem name is not NTFS;
- require remote structure version 1 or 2 and structure size 116;
- bound all text, reject NUL, reject unknown JSON fields and variants, and
  reject any inconsistent outcome/disposition combination;
- expose strict decoding and validation;
- prove the forms through focused positive, negative, cross-field, resource,
  and strict-JSON tests.

Keep the slice effect-free:

- no windows-sys import in production source;
- no unsafe;
- no std::fs, path existence check, handle, FFI, process, environment, clock,
  random, network, persistence, fixture, candidate, or scanner operation;
- no Win32 call;
- no runtime wrapper;
- no topology traversal or receipt issuance;
- no physical platform claim.

The official API assessment is a research input. Its statement that protocol
zero represents absence of a declared remote protocol is explicitly a policy
inference from the nonzero documented WNNC_NET_* provider-family values, not a
quoted Microsoft guarantee. A later physical preflight must invalidate or
revise the policy if target evidence contradicts it.

After this source is processed through SJS and signed, implement one small
machine-form module, export it from cantor_ecosystem, run focused and global
proof, regenerate affected evidence, and complete a support review before
forming any physical Win32-call source.
